The package lance-c provides CMake targets:

    find_package(LanceC CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE LanceC::lance_c)

Consumers require C++17 for lance.hpp. C consumers include lance/lance.h.

The default linkage matches the vcpkg triplet:
    x64-linux         → static  (LanceC::lance_c → LanceC::lance_c_static)
    x64-linux-dynamic → shared  (LanceC::lance_c → LanceC::lance_c_shared)

Override per-build by setting LanceC_LINK=static|shared before find_package.

Prebuilt archives are published for x64-linux, arm64-linux, and arm64-osx.
Other supported vcpkg platforms, including x64-osx, have no matching prebuilt
asset in this release. Install those with the from-source feature:

    vcpkg install 'lance-c[from-source]'

Source builds require a Rust toolchain, CMake, and protoc on the build host.
